---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import PageFooter from '../components/PageFooter.astro';
import Medallion from '../components/Medallion.astro';
import Ornament from '../components/Ornament.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Research and current understanding — CIRWEL Systems"
  description="What CIRWEL is learning about continuity, evidence, runtime interpretation, and accountability across human and software agents."
>
  <PageHeader currentPath="/research" />

  <main class="px-6 lg:px-12 max-w-screen-xl mx-auto">
    <section class="pt-14 pb-20 lg:pt-20 lg:pb-24 border-b border-sepia/50">
      <p class="label text-oxblood mb-6">Research and understanding</p>
      <h1 class="display text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl !leading-[1.08] mb-8 max-w-4xl">Understanding before intervention.</h1>
      <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-stone max-w-3xl">The research asks what information remains useful as work crosses people, processes, and systems—and how that information can support sound next actions.</p>
      <Ornament size="floret" class="mt-10 opacity-80" />
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 grid grid-cols-12 gap-6">
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-4">
        <p class="label text-oxblood mb-4">I · Current understanding</p>
        <Medallion roman="I" class="hidden lg:block mt-7 mb-8" />
        <h2 class="display text-3xl md:text-4xl leading-tight">What the work supports today.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-8 space-y-10">
        <article class="border-t border-oxblood pt-5">
          <h3 class="display text-2xl mb-3">Continuity must be declared.</h3>
          <p class="text-stone leading-relaxed">A reused name is not identity. Explicit process identity and lineage make handoffs reconstructable without pretending two sessions are automatically the same actor.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="border-t border-sepia pt-5">
          <h3 class="display text-2xl mb-3">Evidence matters more than activity.</h3>
          <p class="text-stone leading-relaxed">A large event stream shows that mechanisms are exercised. Tests, reviews, and observed outcomes are what let later agents decide whether a claim deserves trust.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="border-t border-sepia pt-5">
          <h3 class="display text-2xl mb-3">Runtime interpretation remains a research instrument.</h3>
          <p class="text-stone leading-relaxed">Recorded behavioral and operational signals may add useful context, but their value must be established through discrimination, prediction, and intervention studies. Calibration is part of that method, not a product benefit.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 border-t border-sepia/50">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6 mb-10">
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-4"><p class="label text-oxblood">II · Research map</p><Medallion roman="II" class="hidden lg:block mt-7" /></div>
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-8"><h2 class="display text-3xl md:text-5xl leading-tight">Questions, evidence, next work.</h2></div>
      </div>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[720px] border-collapse text-left">
          <thead class="label text-stone">
            <tr class="border-b border-oxblood"><th class="py-4 pr-8 font-normal">Area</th><th class="py-4 pr-8 font-normal">Question</th><th class="py-4 pr-8 font-normal">Where it stands</th><th class="py-4 font-normal">Next useful evidence</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="align-top">
            <tr class="border-b border-sepia/50"><th class="py-6 pr-8 display text-xl font-medium">Continuity</th><td class="py-6 pr-8 text-stone">Can identity, evidence, and decisions survive process changes?</td><td class="py-6 pr-8">Implemented and exercised in CIRWEL’s development environment.</td><td class="py-6 text-stone">Independent deployments and varied handoff conditions.</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-sepia/50"><th class="py-6 pr-8 display text-xl font-medium">Runtime interpretation</th><td class="py-6 pr-8 text-stone">Do recorded state patterns add useful information beyond logs and outputs?</td><td class="py-6 pr-8">Active measurement program; usefulness remains under evaluation.</td><td class="py-6 text-stone">Pre-registered outcome-grounded studies at greater scale.</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-sepia/50"><th class="py-6 pr-8 display text-xl font-medium">Federation</th><td class="py-6 pr-8 text-stone">Can accountability hold across principals without one trusted controller?</td><td class="py-6 pr-8">Protocol and evaluation design exist; multi-host evaluation is next.</td><td class="py-6 text-stone">Adversarial trials across independently controlled infrastructure.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 border-t border-sepia/50 grid grid-cols-12 gap-6">
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-4">
        <p class="label text-oxblood mb-4">III · How the program learns</p>
        <Medallion roman="III" class="hidden lg:block mt-7 mb-8" />
        <h2 class="display text-3xl md:text-4xl leading-tight">Make the next result informative.</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-8 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-10 gap-y-10">
        <div><dt class="display text-2xl mb-3">Ask a bounded question</dt><dd class="text-stone leading-relaxed">Define what would change the current understanding before collecting the decisive evidence.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="display text-2xl mb-3">Ground claims in outcomes</dt><dd class="text-stone leading-relaxed">Connect predictions to what actually happened so confidence can be learned rather than merely reported.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="display text-2xl mb-3">Keep scope visible</dt><dd class="text-stone leading-relaxed">Separate mechanism demonstrations, internal deployment observations, benchmarks, and independent evidence.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="display text-2xl mb-3">Carry understanding forward</dt><dd class="text-stone leading-relaxed">Preserve superseded interpretations in source history while keeping the current public explanation clear.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 border-t border-sepia/50 grid grid-cols-12 gap-6">
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-4"><p class="label text-oxblood">IV · Evidence and participation</p><Medallion roman="IV" class="hidden lg:block mt-7" /></div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-8 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed mb-8">CIRWEL’s deployment is an instrumented development environment, not evidence of external adoption. The most useful contribution is independent evaluation on data and infrastructure CIRWEL does not control.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-4 text-stone">
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19647159">UNITARES paper</a>
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21930161">Federated accountability design</a>
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/hikewa">Datasets and models</a>
          <a href="mailto:founder@cirwel.org">Propose an evaluation</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <PageFooter />
</BaseLayout>
